<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106449" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδρος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>water-snake, Coluber natrix,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.723
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				487a23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				508b1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκὸς ὡς ὕδρου γαστήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Iamb.</u>
					1.218
				</span></i>
			 ( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶδος δράκοντος</span>
			, Sch. in mg.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			a small water-animal, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαλάγγιον</span>
			 or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαῦρος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				4.56
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> the
			constellation <i>Hydra,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eudox.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				2.2.13
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>udrás,</i> O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>oter</i> 'otter'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
